<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Tazes</h1><p class="st-meta">1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Maya province of north-eastern Yucatán, known only from brief mentions in Spanish colonial records.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tazes (Taz) was one of the territories into which northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán</a> split after the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/league-of-mayapan">League of Mayapan</a> around 1441. It lay in the north-east of the peninsula, near the provinces of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cupul">Cupul</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ecab">Ecab</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from a few colonial sources, Tazes seems to have been a group of towns without a strong central ruler. Its people, like their neighbours, farmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and lived in dispersed towns under local batabs.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tazes came under Spanish control during the conquest of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán</a> in the 1540s and was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-yucatan">Province of Yucatán</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tazes.jpg" alt="Tazes" width="320" height="233"><figcaption>Image: Jaontiveros · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cacicazgos_mayas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1441 CE – 1544 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Yucatec Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Taz</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=tazes" aria-label="Tazes on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="1971 1302 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tazes lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2591 1670h0M4910 989h0M2590 1658h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2291 1558h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2291 1558h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mexico. <a href="/atlas?year=1492&amp;focus=tazes">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
